* 2 cans crushed [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* 1 small can of [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]] \n* 2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* 1 medium [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 medium green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]], chopped \n* 1 medium red bell pepper, chopped \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]] or [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chili powder]] \n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]] \n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]], [[Cookbook:Basil|basil]], [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]], or other spice\n\n==Procedure==\n# Heat oil over medium-high heat in a large pot.\n# Add garlic and onion and cook until the onion is translucent (more clear than white). \n# Add peppers and [[Cookbook:Saute|sauté]] for a few minutes. Add crushed tomatoes, tomato paste, and spices. \n# When mixture is bubbling, reduce heat to [[Cookbook:Simmer|simmer]] and add beans. Cover and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for at least 1 hour, stirring occasionally. The longer it simmers, the better it tastes. \n\n== See also ==\n*[[Cookbook:Chili (Vegan)|Chili (Vegan)]]\n*[[Cookbook:Chili_con_carne|Chili con carne]]\n*[[Cookbook:Texas Easy Chili|Texas easy chili]]\n*[[Cookbook:Red Chile Sauce|Red chile sauce]]\n*[[Cookbook:Easy Chili|Easy Chili]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes using black bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chili]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Southwestern recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kidney bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Bean Chili","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"4","ingredi